{"id":185445271,"slug":"proliv-rx-in-the-news","title":"ProLivᵀᴹ Rx in the News!","subtitle":"Podcasts and TV! What a week for at-home difficult-to-treat depression media coverage","post_date":"2026-01-26T14:19:45.877Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/proliv-rx-in-the-news","wordcount":407,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:45:08.452Z","body_sha256":"a5844ce660f1a9e45416499ad7d774a467c0bbc962759b4f2e7ab0af75ed7637","text_words":432,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>It is my pleasure to report that difficult-to-treat depression is having a watershed moment…</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic\" width=\"300\" height=\"267\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:267,&quot;width&quot;:300,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:14470,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/185445271?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!UKkH!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3bb00e3f-b7f0-410b-bef9-ffef0e654b41_300x267.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Dr. Linda Carpenter</figcaption></figure></div><p>First, the Carlat Psychiatry Podcast featured Dr. Linda Carpetner, the Principal Investigator on <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1935861X25003158\">the MOOD study</a>.</p><div class=\"apple-podcast-container\" data-component-name=\"ApplePodcastToDom\"><iframe class=\"apple-podcast \" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000745706519&quot;,&quot;isEpisode&quot;:true,&quot;imageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/podcast-episode_1000745706519.jpg&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;ProLivRx: A New Approval in Depression&quot;,&quot;podcastTitle&quot;:&quot;The Carlat Psychiatry Podcast&quot;,&quot;podcastByline&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:1250000,&quot;numEpisodes&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;targetUrl&quot;:&quot;https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/prolivrx-a-new-approval-in-depression/id1463414537?i=1000745706519&amp;uo=4&quot;,&quot;releaseDate&quot;:&quot;2026-01-19T07:00:00Z&quot;}\" src=\"https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000745706519\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay *; encrypted-media *;\" allowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe></div><p>Today, Chris Aiken follow up with an story about the interaction between Afferent Sensory stimulation in depression, such as ProLivᵀᴹ Rx.</p><div class=\"apple-podcast-container\" data-component-name=\"ApplePodcastToDom\"><iframe class=\"apple-podcast \" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000746656253&quot;,&quot;isEpisode&quot;:true,&quot;imageUrl&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/podcast-episode_1000746656253.jpg&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;ProLivRx: How it Works&quot;,&quot;podcastTitle&quot;:&quot;The Carlat Psychiatry Podcast&quot;,&quot;podcastByline&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;:753000,&quot;numEpisodes&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;targetUrl&quot;:&quot;https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/prolivrx-how-it-works/id1463414537?i=1000746656253&amp;uo=4&quot;,&quot;releaseDate&quot;:&quot;2026-01-26T07:00:00Z&quot;}\" src=\"https://embed.podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/id1463414537?i=1000746656253\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay *; encrypted-media *;\" allowfullscreen=\"true\"></iframe></div><p>As someone who works as CMO at <a href=\"https://neurolief.com\">Neurolief</a>, the study sponsor of the MOOD study, I’m excited for a world where more thinkers, reporters, and investigators to continue to dig in to the mechanisms by which brain stimulation work.</p><p>As if this wasn’t enough coverage, she was <strong>featured on the news</strong> (WJAR 10) just last night!  <a href=\"https://turnto10.com/features/health-landing-page/take-home-device-expands-treatment-drug-resistant-depression-brain-scans-doctors-nurse-mood-disorder-january-21-2026\">Watch it here.</a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://neurolief.com/#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dpopup%3Aopen%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6IjMzNyIsInRvZ2dsZSI6ZmFsc2V9&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Get More Information about ProLiv Rx&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://neurolief.com/#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dpopup%3Aopen%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6IjMzNyIsInRvZ2dsZSI6ZmFsc2V9\"><span>Get More Information about ProLiv Rx</span></a></p><p>Over at Radial, we have <a href=\"https://www.meetradial.com/blog/neuromodulation-therapy\">this quick explainer</a> about the full range of neuromodulation treatments.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg\" width=\"1456\" height=\"479\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:479,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:279434,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Muir wears ProLivᵀᴹ Rx&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/jpeg&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/185445271?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Dr. Owen Muir wears ProLivᵀᴹ Rx\" title=\"Dr. Owen Muir wears ProLivᵀᴹ Rx\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IUQq!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb3d41b19-bca7-4c3f-8f43-8bd84397e51d_2224x732.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Dr. Owen Muir wearing ProLivᵀᴹ Rx on stage at RAMHT-AI. </figcaption></figure></div><p>Is it a big deal?  Well, it’s a drug-free adjunctive treatment, <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1935861X25003158\">with the following outcomes in an RCT,</a> that can be administered at home:</p><blockquote><p>Compared to sham treatment, participants receiving active treatment had significantly higher remission rates (21.3 % vs 6.0 %, <em>p</em> = 0.027) and achieved significantly more shifts to lower HDRS17 depression severity categories. Participants further improved during the subsequent eight weeks of open-label active stimulation with a mean reduction of almost 10 points from baseline and achieved a remission rate of 32 %.</p></blockquote><p>Chris Aiken, on the <a href=\"https://www.thecarlatreport.com/blogs/2-the-carlat-psychiatry-podcast/post/5827-prolivrx-how-it-works\">Carlat Psychiatry podcast</a>, adds some color to the dry data above in his recent podcast:</p><blockquote><p>Before ProLivRx, the other recent approval was the Flow device. All of the devices we use in psychiatry were just cleared. TMS was cleared. ECT just cleared. We don't know how ProLivRx works, but we do know how it operates, by stimulating the sensory nerves, the occipital and trigeminal nerves. Think of it as an electrical massage of the face and head. The trigeminal nerve is the sensory nerve for the face, and the occipital nerve runs down the neck, encoding sensation for the back of the head, the top of the head, and around the ears. Our best guess of how ProLivRx works is that stimulating these sensory nerves has downstream effects in the brain, enhancing blood flow and reorganizing neurotransmitters and synaptic connections in parts of the brain that keep us alert and awake, the reticular activating system, and that regulate actions and emotions, like the locus coeruleus, the cingulate cortex, and that deep well of serotonin in the brain, the raphe nuclei.</p></blockquote><p>Thanks for reading.  It’s really getting fun to write about Brain Medicine!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/proliv-rx-in-the-news?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/proliv-rx-in-the-news?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>","text":"It is my pleasure to report that difficult-to-treat depression is having a watershed moment…\n\nDr. Linda Carpenter\n\nFirst, the Carlat Psychiatry Podcast featured Dr. Linda Carpetner, the Principal Investigator on the MOOD study .\n\nToday, Chris Aiken follow up with an story about the interaction between Afferent Sensory stimulation in depression, such as ProLivᵀᴹ Rx.\n\nAs someone who works as CMO at Neurolief , the study sponsor of the MOOD study, I’m excited for a world where more thinkers, reporters, and investigators to continue to dig in to the mechanisms by which brain stimulation work.\n\nAs if this wasn’t enough coverage, she was featured on the news (WJAR 10) just last night! Watch it here.\n\nGet More Information about ProLiv Rx\n\nOver at Radial, we have this quick explainer about the full range of neuromodulation treatments.\n\nDr. Owen Muir wearing ProLivᵀᴹ Rx on stage at RAMHT-AI.\n\nIs it a big deal? Well, it’s a drug-free adjunctive treatment, with the following outcomes in an RCT, that can be administered at home:\n\nCompared to sham treatment, participants receiving active treatment had significantly higher remission rates (21.3 % vs 6.0 %, p = 0.027) and achieved significantly more shifts to lower HDRS17 depression severity categories. Participants further improved during the subsequent eight weeks of open-label active stimulation with a mean reduction of almost 10 points from baseline and achieved a remission rate of 32 %.\n\nChris Aiken, on the Carlat Psychiatry podcast , adds some color to the dry data above in his recent podcast:\n\nBefore ProLivRx, the other recent approval was the Flow device. All of the devices we use in psychiatry were just cleared. TMS was cleared. ECT just cleared. We don't know how ProLivRx works, but we do know how it operates, by stimulating the sensory nerves, the occipital and trigeminal nerves. Think of it as an electrical massage of the face and head. The trigeminal nerve is the sensory nerve for the face, and the occipital nerve runs down the neck, encoding sensation for the back of the head, the top of the head, and around the ears. Our best guess of how ProLivRx works is that stimulating these sensory nerves has downstream effects in the brain, enhancing blood flow and reorganizing neurotransmitters and synaptic connections in parts of the brain that keep us alert and awake, the reticular activating system, and that regulate actions and emotions, like the locus coeruleus, the cingulate cortex, and that deep well of serotonin in the brain, the raphe nuclei.\n\nThanks for reading. It’s really getting fun to write about Brain Medicine!\n\nShare\n\nSubscribe now"}